# Fixtures are inputs to assertions: reformatting their markup changes the text
# nodes, whitespace, and nth-child structure the tests measure.
tests/fixtures/

# Authoritative inputs, not deliverables. The spec and the plan are quoted
# verbatim by README.md and docs/data-contract.md, so a formatter must not
# rewrite them.
plans/
docs/superpowers/specs/

# The TypeScript and build scripts are hand-formatted on purpose: compact
# allowlist tables, aligned trailing comments that explain WHY a line reads the
# way it does, and blocks that match the implementation plan verbatim. Prettier
# reflows all three (a 15-entry allowlist becomes 15 lines and the comments
# detach from what they annotate), so the formatter owns prose and data files
# and ESLint owns the code.
*.ts
*.mts
*.mjs
*.js
